# Amber — voice WebSocket at /ws, MCP streamable HTTP at /mcp, health at /health.
#
# ONE reverse_proxy covers all three. Caddy v2 proxies an `Upgrade: websocket`
# request transparently: no @ws matcher, no header_up Connection, none of the nginx
# ritual. Adding an explicit @ws block is not merely unnecessary, it is a footgun —
# `reverse_proxy @ws ...` followed by a bare `reverse_proxy ...` creates two
# handlers with different option sets, and whichever one you forgot to configure is
# the one that will drop your streaming settings.
#
# The upstream is a loopback port, which is true whether Amber runs in a container
# (she does now) or under systemd — see install/README.md.

amber.johnny.dev {
	import common amber

	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000 {
		import streaming
	}
}
